{
  "$comment": "Which operations are promoted to first-class tools, and what they are called. Read by both servers \u2014 mcp/src/manifest.ts (the local stdio server) and app/mcp/ (the hosted one) \u2014 because curation is a product decision and two copies of it would drift. Everything else about a tool (input schema, description, the HTTP call) is generated from the OpenAPI spec. Not all 161 operations: every client caps the tool list \u2014 Cursor around 40, Junie 100, Copilot 128 \u2014 so a small promoted set covers the common path and find_operation reaches the rest on demand.",
  "groups": {
    "rendering": "The product.",
    "checking": "Checking without rendering. Cheaper than a render and the right first move for an agent: catches a bad document before it costs a render off the account's quota.",
